Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:03.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Once upon a time in ancient China,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.00,0:00:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,there lived a legendary archer named Hou Yi
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.48,0:00:09.48,Default,,0,0,0,,and his wife, Chang'e.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.18,0:00:11.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Hou Yi was a hero.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.44,0:00:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,When ten blazing suns once scorched the Earth,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.52,0:00:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,he shot down nine of them and saved the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.74,0:00:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,For this heroic deed,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.72,0:00:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the Queen Mother of the West gave him an\Nextraordinary reward:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.76,0:00:31.64,Default,,0,0,0,,a magical medicine called the elixir of immortality.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.98,0:00:35.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoever drank it would become an immortal —
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.88,0:00:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,a magical being who could live forever beyond the\Nmortal world.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.22,0:00:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,But there was enough for only one person.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.76,0:00:47.64,Default,,0,0,0,,If Hou Yi drank it and became immortal,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.10,0:00:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,he would have to leave the human world behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.74,0:00:54.08,Default,,0,0,0,,And that meant leaving Chang'e behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.70,0:00:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,So he chose not to drink it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.78,0:01:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, he asked Chang'e to keep the elixir safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.46,0:01:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,But one day, while Hou Yi was away,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.82,0:01:10.02,Default,,0,0,0,,one of his apprentices, Pang Meng, tried to steal\Nit.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.68,0:01:12.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Chang'e couldn’t let him have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.28,0:01:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,With no time to lose, she made a desperate choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.40,0:01:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,She drank it herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Almost at once, she began to rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.20,0:01:25.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The elixir had made her immortal!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.56,0:01:29.58,Default,,0,0,0,,She could no longer remain in the human world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.32,0:01:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Higher and higher she floated —
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.16,0:01:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,above the house, above the mountains, and into the\Nnight sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.28,0:01:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,But Chang'e still loved Hou Yi.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.58,0:01:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,She wanted to stay as close to him as she could.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.90,0:01:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,So she chose the Moon —
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.00,0:01:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,the nearest place in the heavens to the human world\Nbelow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.32,0:01:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,When Hou Yi returned and learned what had happened,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.20,0:01:58.52,Default,,0,0,0,,he was heartbroken.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.60,0:02:03.26,Default,,0,0,0,,That night, he looked up at the bright full moon
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.30,0:02:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and thought of Chang'e.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.50,0:02:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,He set out fruits and cakes beneath the moonlight,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.66,0:02:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,as if he could still share them with her from far\Naway.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.14,0:02:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,And that was how the Mid-Autumn Festival began.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.52,0:02:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.68,0:02:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.96,0:02:25.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that really where the Mid-Autumn Festival came\Nfrom?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.76,0:02:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.96,0:02:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s the legend.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.38,0:02:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Real history is a little messier.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.80,0:02:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Festivals aren’t always invented.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.76,0:02:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes, they grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.31,0:02:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Mid-Autumn grew from several old traditions
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.37,0:02:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,that slowly came together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.69,0:02:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,For most of Chinese history,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.97,0:02:50.11,Default,,0,0,0,,people’s lives depended heavily on farming.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.73,0:02:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,They had to watch the seasons carefully —
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.83,0:02:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,when to plant, when the rains were likely to come,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.67,0:02:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,and when crops were ready to harvest.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.33,0:03:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,So autumn, the harvest season,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.61,0:03:03.59,Default,,0,0,0,,naturally became a time to celebrate what had been\Ngathered,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.09,0:03:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,perform seasonal rituals, and pray for good harvests\Nto come.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.13,0:03:09.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But why the Moon?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.87,0:03:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Ancient Chinese people kept track of time by\Nwatching both the Sun and the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.39,0:03:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The traditional Chinese calendar followed both.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.67,0:03:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The Sun helped keep the calendar aligned with the\Nseasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.07,0:03:23.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The Moon shaped the months.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.41,0:03:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Around the middle of each month,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.25,0:03:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,the Moon becomes full.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.41,0:03:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And long before the Mid-Autumn Festival existed in\Nthe form we know today,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.59,0:03:36.49,Default,,0,0,0,,people in China were already holding autumn rituals\Nto honour the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.91,0:03:40.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Over many centuries, harvest traditions,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.77,0:03:44.81,Default,,0,0,0,,rituals honouring the Moon, moon-gazing, poetry,\Nfood,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.15,0:03:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and stories like Chang'e gradually came together.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.17,0:03:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,By the Tang and Song dynasties,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.59,0:03:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,something recognisably like today’s Mid-Autumn\NFestival had taken shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.25,0:04:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So no — the festival probably did not begin because\NChang'e flew to the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.55,0:04:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But her story stayed,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.29,0:04:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,because it captured something people felt deeply.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.09,0:04:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And that feeling would become the heart of\NMid-Autumn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.97,0:04:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,So what does Mid-Autumn actually look like today?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.26,0:04:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,First, people come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.96,0:04:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,More than anything else,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.90,0:04:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mid-Autumn is a festival of reunion.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.12,0:04:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And in Chinese culture,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.78,0:04:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,family is often thought of across generations,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.98,0:04:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,not just as one household.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.50,0:04:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That can mean grandparents, parents, grown-up\Nchildren, brothers and sisters —
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.94,0:04:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,sometimes aunts, uncles, and cousins too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.02,0:04:46.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Several generations come back to the same table.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.92,0:04:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And once they do, a pattern starts to appear.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.78,0:04:53.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The same shape keeps showing up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.06,0:04:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,A full moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.74,0:04:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,A round mooncake.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.90,0:05:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,A family gathered in a circle around the dinner\Ntable.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.60,0:05:05.80,Default,,0,0,0,,In Chinese, yuan means round.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.20,0:05:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,And roundness carries the idea of being whole,\Ncomplete.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.40,0:05:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And that same yuan appears in tuanyuan — reunion:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.68,0:05:19.70,Default,,0,0,0,,people who belong together, together again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.58,0:05:22.26,Default,,0,0,0,,A full moon is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.78,0:05:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,No piece is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.86,0:05:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And a family feels complete in much the same way:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.40,0:05:29.78,Default,,0,0,0,,when no one is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.56,0:05:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,That is why the full moon became such a powerful\Nsymbol of reunion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.58,0:05:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,And that idea of reunion is everywhere in the\Nfestival.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.74,0:05:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Families sit down for a reunion dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.56,0:05:45.06,Default,,0,0,0,,They cut and share round mooncakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.68,0:05:47.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And when night falls, they go outside —
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.32,0:05:52.12,Default,,0,0,0,,or simply look out of a window — to admire the full\Nmoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.16,0:05:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,In many parts of China,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.96,0:05:58.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Mid-Autumn also arrives with the scent of osmanthus\N—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.78,0:06:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,tiny golden flowers that bloom in autumn.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.26,0:06:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,People admire them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.06,0:06:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,flavour sweets and tea with them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.94,0:06:08.78,Default,,0,0,0,,and traditionally even make osmanthus wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.60,0:06:11.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And China is a big place,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.90,0:06:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,so different regions have traditions of their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.02,0:06:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,In some parts of China,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.68,0:06:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,children may carry lanterns or solve lantern\Nriddles.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.60,0:06:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,In Shanghai, Mid-Autumn tables traditionally include\Nduck, taro, and edamame.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.12,0:06:31.28,Default,,0,0,0,,And in Hong Kong, a great fire dragon dances through\Nthe streets
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.32,0:06:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,in a blaze of light and incense.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.36,0:06:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,But Mid-Autumn isn’t only about the people who made\Nit home.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.60,0:06:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It is also about the ones who couldn’t.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.00,0:06:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,For centuries, people have spent Mid-Autumn
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.92,0:06:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,far away from those they love —
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.16,0:06:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,away from parents, grandparents, children,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.08,0:06:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,or the place they think of as home.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.28,0:06:57.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And when that happens,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.32,0:07:00.22,Default,,0,0,0,,people look up at the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.64,0:07:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Because somewhere far away,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.26,0:07:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the people they love are under that same Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.84,0:07:11.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The Moon becomes more than something beautiful in\Nthe sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.60,0:07:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It becomes a way to remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.34,0:07:16.68,Default,,0,0,0,,A way to miss someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.88,0:07:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,A way to feel close across a great distance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.22,0:07:26.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And maybe that is why the story of Chang'e never\Ndisappeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.08,0:07:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The legend probably did not create the festival.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.56,0:07:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But perhaps it stayed with the festival
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.78,0:07:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,because, at its heart, it is also a story about\Nseparation —
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.96,0:07:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and the wish to be together again.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.60,0:07:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Hou Yi on Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.24,0:07:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Chang'e on the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.86,0:07:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Far apart, and still looking toward one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.08,0:07:52.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The full moon is whole because nothing is missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.18,0:07:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,A family feels whole for the same reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.16,0:07:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,And when someone is missing,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.88,0:08:00.96,Default,,0,0,0,,we look up, remember them,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.14,0:08:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,and know that the same Moon shines over them too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.60,0:08:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,月圆，人团圆。\NWhen the Moon is full, may the family be whole.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.06,0:08:13.60,Default,,0,0,0,,And wherever the people you love are,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.14,0:08:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,may you be together again soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.30,0:08:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.\N中秋快乐！
